Overview:\par
This document captures the conversation and actions taken from requirements analysis through implementation, testing, and PR creation for the "payment-status" prototype in the Invoice-Generator repository. It includes design decisions, code changes, tests, CI/E2E attempts, troubleshooting notes, and the final PR creation steps.
\par
\b 1) Requirements & Architecture (summary)\b0\par
- Goal: add payment-status handling, audit trail, overdue scheduler, admin-only status changes, and automated verification (API Jest tests, UI Playwright E2E).\par
- Prototype persistence: file-based JSON under `api/data/`. Production recommendation: Postgres audit table with partitioning and retention.\par
- Auth placeholder: header-based `x-user-role`/`x-user-id` used in prototype; must be replaced with JWT/OIDC in production.\par
\par
\b 2) Implementation Summary\b0\par
- Files modified/added (feature/payment-status branch):\par
  - `api/routes/invoices.js`: added `paymentStatus`, `partial`, `version`, admin PATCH endpoint to change status and append audit entries.\par
  - `api/utils/store.js`: added `appendAudit`, read/write helpers for `api/data/audit_log.json`.\par
  - `api/scheduler/markOverdue.js`: new script to mark `Unpaid` invoices as `Overdue` after 15 days, appending audit entries (system user).\par
  - `api/data/audit_log.json`: initial audit store (JSON array).\par
  - `api/test/api.test.js` and `api/test/markOverdue.test.js`: Jest integration tests validating creation defaults, admin-only patch behaviour, and scheduler behaviour.\par
  - `ui/tests/e2e.spec.js` and `ui/playwright.config.cjs`: Playwright E2E test and config (expects API and UI servers to be externally started).\par
\par
\b 3) Testing & Results\b0\par
- API Jest tests: ran in `api/` with `npm.cmd test --silent`. Result:\par
  PASS  test/markOverdue.test.js\par
  PASS  test/api.test.js\par
  Test Suites: 2 passed, 2 total\par
  Tests: 6 passed, 6 total\par
- UI Playwright E2E: tests present but unstable in this environment. Failures encountered included process spawn errors (ENOENT / EINVAL) when tests attempted to spawn servers, and a later timeout waiting for `http://localhost:5173/`.\par
\par
\b 4) Security & Operational Notes\b0\par
- Critical: `.mcp.json` contained a Jira API token and should be rotated and removed from the repo.\par
- Production concerns: file-based audit storage is not scalable/atomic; DB-backed audit with partitions is recommended. Add optimistic locking enforcement (409) and audit-query endpoints before production use. Add proper auth (JWT/OIDC) and RBAC mapping.\par
\par
